<BaseLayout title="Personal Intelligence Refinery — Governed AI-assisted research" description="A private, local-first governed system for turning untrusted material into grounded decision support with deterministic validation and explicit human authority.">
  <article class="pir-case-study">
    <header class="pir-hero shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Strong secondary system · private, local-first</p>
      <h1>Personal Intelligence<br />Refinery</h1>
      <p class="pir-subtitle">A governed AI-assisted corridor for turning untrusted external material into grounded, human-authorized decision support.</p>
      <div class="pir-hero-grid"><p>Plausible model output should not automatically become trusted system knowledge. PIR separates probabilistic model reasoning from deterministic validation and human authority before any material may become a durable claim.</p><dl class="pir-facts"><div><dt>Matthew’s role</dt><dd>Operating-model, provenance, authority, validation, and provider-contract design</dd></div><div><dt>Current boundary</dt><dd>Private, local-first system; bounded hosted-model validation only</dd></div></dl></div>
      <p class="pir-cta"><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/matthew-ralph-work-samples/tree/main/personal-intelligence-refinery">View curated work sample <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
      <aside class="authority-ledger authority-ledger-pir" aria-label="Personal Intelligence Refinery authority ledger"><p class="eyebrow">Authority ledger</p><div><section><strong>System did</strong><span>Ground and validate CandidateClaims.</span></section><section><strong>Matthew directed</strong><span>Provenance model, provider contract, validation, and value test.</span></section><section><strong>Human authority remained</strong><span>ACCEPT, EDIT_AND_ACCEPT, REJECT, or DEFER.</span></section></div></aside>
    </header>

    <section class="pir-section shell" aria-labelledby="pir-problem"><div class="pir-label"><p class="eyebrow">01 · Problem</p></div><div class="pir-body"><h2 id="pir-problem">Useful information is not automatically trustworthy enough to guide a decision.</h2><p class="pir-lead">External material can contain valuable signals alongside ambiguity, opinion, or instructions that should not control a system. PIR creates a controlled refinery between that material and any durable decision support.</p></div></section>

    <section class="pir-section shell" aria-labelledby="pir-system"><div class="pir-label"><p class="eyebrow">02 · System</p></div><div class="pir-body"><h2 id="pir-system">A model may propose. The system validates. A human authorizes.</h2><ol class="pir-flow" aria-label="Personal Intelligence Refinery governed flow"><li>External material</li><li>Extracted source evidence</li><li>Model proposes CandidateClaim</li><li>PIR grounds and validates</li><li>Human accepts, edits, rejects, or defers</li><li>Only approved material may become a durable Claim</li></ol><p class="pir-note"><strong>CandidateClaim is not a Claim.</strong> A model cannot directly promote a proposal into a durable governed record.</p></div></section>

    <section class="pir-ledger shell" aria-label="Bounded V008 evidence at a glance"><article><p class="eyebrow">Coverage</p><strong>5 / 5</strong><span>Frozen expected material spans covered</span></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Grounding</p><strong>0</strong><span>Grounding violations in this fixture</span></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Human authority</p><strong>5 / 1</strong><span>ACCEPT decisions / REJECT decision</span></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Operator judgment</p><strong>YES</strong><span>Manual claim-identification work reduced</span></article></section>

    <section class="pir-section shell" aria-labelledby="pir-proof"><div class="pir-label"><p class="eyebrow">03 · Real-model proof</p></div><div class="pir-body"><h2 id="pir-proof">A bounded test showed value without surrendering the decision boundary.</h2><p>V008 used five frozen public-safe synthetic fixtures. The hosted model returned five structured responses across five calls with no retries, yielding six valid CandidateClaims. All final candidates passed the unchanged production validator.</p><div class="pir-proof-grid"><div><strong>Exact grounding</strong><span>Supporting excerpts had to match their attested source segments exactly and uniquely. PIR derived offsets deterministically; no fuzzy quote repair was allowed.</span></div><div><strong>Human review</strong><span>Five candidates were accepted. “Best option for everyone.” was rejected, showing that valid structured output is not automatically approved knowledge.</span></div><div><strong>Bounded cost</strong><span>$0.002041 of hosted-model spend was reconciled against a one-time $0.05 experiment ceiling.</span></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="pir-section shell" aria-labelledby="pir-correction"><div class="pir-label"><p class="eyebrow">04 · Failure → correction</p></div><div class="pir-body"><h2 id="pir-correction">Observability exposed a contract mismatch; validation did not get weaker.</h2><div class="pir-chronology"><div><p class="eyebrow">V006</p><strong>Inference worked; safe diagnostics were insufficient.</strong></div><div><p class="eyebrow">V007</p><strong>Observability revealed the model was being asked to generate PIR-owned fields.</strong></div><div><p class="eyebrow">V008</p><strong>The model generated semantic content; PIR retained identity, offsets, enum constraints, and validation.</strong></div></div><p class="pir-note">The production validator was <strong>not weakened</strong> to accommodate the provider integration.</p></div></section>

    <section class="pir-section shell" aria-labelledby="pir-control"><div class="pir-label"><p class="eyebrow">05 · Provenance + control</p></div><div class="pir-body"><h2 id="pir-control">Decision integrity depends on the boundaries around the model.</h2><div class="pir-control-grid"><div><strong>Evidence integrity</strong><span>Claim and evidence remain separate; source excerpts are grounded before review.</span></div><div><strong>Deterministic controls</strong><span>System-owned identity, accepted constraints, offsets, and validation remain outside model discretion.</span></div><div><strong>Human authority</strong><span>Every valid CandidateClaim requires ACCEPT, EDIT_AND_ACCEPT, REJECT, or DEFER.</span></div><div><strong>Bounded execution</strong><span>Privacy, egress, and experiment-level spend controls constrain the validation harness.</span></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="pir-section shell" aria-labelledby="pir-role"><div class="pir-label"><p class="eyebrow">06 · Matthew’s role</p></div><div class="pir-body"><h2 id="pir-role">Designing the authority model, not presenting model output as authority.</h2><p>Matthew designed the refinery’s operating model, provenance and authority boundaries, deterministic validation strategy, provider/system contract, and real-model value test; directed bounded implementation and failure investigation; and retained human authority over promotion of model proposals into durable claims.</p></div></section>

    <section class="pir-section shell" aria-labelledby="pir-boundary"><div class="pir-label"><p class="eyebrow">07 · Boundary</p></div><div class="pir-body"><h2 id="pir-boundary">Bounded evidence, not a production AI platform claim.</h2><div class="pir-boundaries"><div><p class="eyebrow">What the test supports</p><ul><li>Grounded CandidateClaim proposals from five synthetic fixtures</li><li>Deterministic validation and explicit human review</li><li>Experiment-level cost control and a bounded injection fixture</li></ul></div><div><p class="eyebrow">What it does not prove</p><ul><li>Autonomous research or automatic fact verification</li><li>Routine hosted inference, enterprise deployment, or full evidence adjudication</li><li>General prompt-injection resistance or production operating cost</li></ul></div></div><p class="pir-note">The bounded synthetic injection fixture passed without changing tool access, routing, authority, privacy, spend, or schema behavior. It is not a claim of general injection immunity.</p></div></section>

    <section class="pir-evidence shell" aria-labelledby="pir-evidence"><p class="eyebrow">08 · Public evidence</p><h2 id="pir-evidence">Inspect the curated public evidence.</h2><p>The canonical implementation remains private. The public work sample documents the bounded proof and its limits without exposing private source material or operational records.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/matthew-ralph-work-samples/tree/main/personal-intelligence-refinery">View curated work sample <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  </article>
